# ⌘F on the lists shows the search field with the focus in it, typing narrows the lists as it
# goes, Esc clears the search and goes back to the list, and Esc again hides the field, as
# LOUPE_SNAPSHOT_SEARCH does.
wait settled
open lists
expect search missing
expect button in list 1 count >1

press cmd+f
expect search is focused

# The viewer (glenjamin) is the author of every PR in Mine, so their login keeps them all.
type "glenjamin"
expect search has value "glenjamin"
expect text ~"No pull requests match" missing
expect button in list 1 count >1
snap search-mine

press esc
expect search has value ""
expect list 1 is focused
press esc
wait until search missing

# Something no PR has: both lists empty out and say so, and Esc brings them back.
press cmd+f
type "zz-no-such-pull-request"
expect text ~"No pull requests match" exists
expect button in list missing
snap search-nothing
press esc
expect search has value ""
expect button in list 1 count >1
press esc
wait until search missing
snap search-cleared
